{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 41 (chapter 4, The Wild Heart), at night. Deep wolf country: the player village in the west, a sneaky rival on a crag walled by cliffs in the east (disc aboveSea 104, falloff 2) that no army climbs until objective 3, when six shape steps raise a stone stair on its west face, so the rival lives until its stage. Stage 1 clear the three dens within 34 cells of the village (8, 7 and 7 wolves; the road den also stands in the forest road area so the validator sees a setup den there); an idle village falls to four warden scouts landing on the south shore every 120 s from 480 s (until 0). Stage 2 the dormant moon stone (reliquary, 6 followers, 60 s) wakes; 8 wolves guard the hill and 6 more spill out when your people near it; it teaches the Fire Lodge. Stage 3 the prayer spawns the pack mother's great den (28 wolves) on the forest road at once, and kin packs of 8 den north and south of it 20 and 50 s later (warned); clearDens fromStage with no n counts every den in the road area, so the kin count once they land. Stage 4 survive 420 s while 6 wardens and 2 firecallers march from the east foot and 4 wardens slip through the north woods every 70 s (warned, until 3). Stage 5 the stair rises and the rival musters 5 wardens at its head every 60 s (warned, until 4) on top of 18 posted wardens, 6 firecallers and 3 towers. Measured with the hard aggressive bot: offset 2 stages done near ticks 7214, 11014, 15040, 23439, 34304; offsets 0 to 5 win at 25117, 24393, 34304, 35095, 24535, 31818 (the crag fight either breaks at once or grinds through several musters). Time limit 3600 s (72000 ticks).",
